  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n33(1/3)% of 900 liters\n\n14(2/7)% of 490 liters\n\n**Formula Used:**\n\nPercentage value = (Percentage ÷ 100) × Quantity\n\n33(1/3)% = 100 ÷ 3\n\n14(2/7)% = (14 × 7 + 2) ÷ 7 = 100 ÷ 7\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n⇒ 33(1/3)% = 100 ÷ 3 = 33.33%\n\n⇒ 14(2/7)% = 100 ÷ 7 = 14.2857%\n\n⇒ (33(1/3) ÷ 100) × 900 = (100 ÷ 3 ÷ 100) × 900 = (1 ÷ 3) × 900 = 300 liters\n\n⇒ (14(2/7) ÷ 100) × 490 = (100 ÷ 7 ÷ 100) × 490 = (1 ÷ 7) × 490 = 70 liters\n\n⇒ Total = 300 + 70 = 370 liters\n\n**∴ The correct answer is 370 liters.**",
